    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1291">

                <pb facs="1051" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6331/12–649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-06">December 6,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received December 6—8:29 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2210. Ward states was asked yesterday (December 5) by local authorities for
                    recent deeds or leases (uncertain which) for two pieces <pb facs="1052" n="1042"
                        xml:id="pg1042"/> Government real estate Mukden. When Ward stated believed
                    title deeds in Washington, was informed US Government ownership would not be
                    recognized.</p>
                <p>Ward has had no further contact with Steventon, British pro-Consul Mukden, re
                    takeover property.</p>
                <p>Bryners now removing personal property and moveable Government property.</p>
                <p>Tientsin by mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
